.TH EVENTHORIZON 1 "September 2026" "eventhorizon 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
eventhorizon, eh \- black hole widget for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eventhorizon
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B eh
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B eventhorizon
draws Luminet's 1979 plot of a black hole live in the terminal: a thin
accretion disk around a Schwarzschild black hole, its light bent by gravity,
turning at true Keplerian rates so the picture never repeats.
.PP
In terminals that answer the kitty graphics protocol, such as kitty and
Ghostty, it draws in real pixels; elsewhere it uses braille dots. It fills the
window and follows it when resized.
.PP
The first run solves a bank of 31 lensing maps in the background, about a
minute, kept in \fI~/.cache/eventhorizon\fR. Until then, tilt, zoom and mass
move a step at a time.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B h ?
List every key.
.TP
.B q Esc
Quit.
.TP
.B 1\-9 0 < >
Pick a preset, a random one, or step through them all.
.TP
.B +
Save the current look as a preset.
.TP
.B X X
Delete the current preset; a copy is kept in \fIdeleted\-presets.toml\fR.
.TP
.B [ ] \- = , .
Inclination, disk size and mass.
.TP
.B p b k
Palette, bloom and glow palette.
.TP
.B ! @ # $ I A
A probe, a transmission, the observatory HUD, a warp jump (again to return),
invert, and events on their own.
.TP
.B Tab
Show or hide the status line.
.SH OPTIONS
Run
.B eventhorizon \-\-help
for the full list, grouped. Options typed on the command line win over the
preset opened at start.
.TP
.BI \-\-preset " name"
Open with a preset by name, or \fBrandom\fR, \fBfirst\fR or \fBnone\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-pixels \-\-no\-pixels
Force pixels or braille instead of detecting.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/eventhorizon/config.toml
Settings, written once with comments and never rewritten: start preset, frame
rates focused and unfocused, status line, pixels, events, transmissions.
.TP
.I ~/.config/eventhorizon/presets.toml
Presets, managed by the app.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/eventhorizon/
The bank of lensing maps.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR luminet (1)
.SH AUTHORS
Meow\-Ludo, on luminet by Bjorge Meulemeester.
